# {{ .Name }} ({{ .Type }})

> **Requires Portainer Business Edition 3.1 or later.** On Community Edition or an older server the apply fails with an error that says so.

**Portainer Business Edition 3.1.0 serves the OIDC provider only when started with the `oidc` feature flag**: `--feat=oidc` (or the environment variable `FEATURE_FLAG=oidc`; Helm chart: `--set "feature.flags[0]=--feat=oidc"`). Without it every OIDC API call fails with an error that says so.

Ends every session of a client of Portainer's OIDC provider, or only one user's sessions in it. Their tokens are revoked at once.

> **See also:** the [`portainer_oidc_client_sessions_end` action](../actions/oidc_client_sessions_end.md) (Terraform >= 1.14) runs the same operation on demand or from a lifecycle `action_trigger`, without a resource in state.

## Example Usage

```hcl
resource "portainer_oidc_client_sessions_end" "this" {
  client_id = tonumber(portainer_oidc_client.grafana.id)
  user_id   = var.user_id

  triggers = {
    reason = var.reason
  }
}
```

{{ .SchemaMarkdown | trimspace }}

## Attributes Reference

This resource exports no attributes beyond its `id`.

## Lifecycle & Behavior

It is a one-shot operation: every argument forces it to run again, and without a `triggers` value the resource runs once and then stays put. Destroying it only removes it from state.
